===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[concise]] [[summary]] of a current situation.
#: {{cot|en|press gaggle}}
#: {{ux|en|The president received a '''briefing''' on the situation before going to the press conference.}}
# A [[meeting]] to [[share]] a concise summary of a current situation, especially in close [[preparation]] for an [[operation]] or [[undertaking]].
#: {{ux|en|Today's '''briefing''' of the press will take place at 10 o'clock.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=September 22 2021|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/58643421|author=w:Guillem Balagué|work=BBC Sport|title=Barcelona: The toxic battle ripping apart a European giant|passage=Despite knowing that getting rid of Koeman was going to necessitate putting his hand very deep into what are currently very shallow pockets, Laporta changed tack a couple of weeks ago by summoning journalists for an off-the-record '''briefing''' about what was going to happen with the coach.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260509180126/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/58643421|archivedate=9 May 2026}}

